# CarePlan Scheduler — Cline project rules

These rules apply to every task in this repository. Read them before every task.

## What this project is
CarePlan Scheduler is a standalone, multi-tenant scheduling app for Missouri home and
community-based services (HCBS). Phase 1 builds only the rules engine: a pure TypeScript
package with no UI, in `packages/engine`. The full specification is `docs/ENGINE-SPEC.md`.
That file is the source of truth. If a prompt and the spec disagree, stop and ask.

## Hard rules
1. Build exactly what the current prompt asks. Do not start the next task, add UI, add
   Firebase, or refactor files the prompt did not name.
2. Every rule function is named after its spec ID (e.g. `ruleSCH08CalendarCheck`) and has a
   JSDoc line: `@rule SCH-08` and `@source <source named in the spec>`.
3. Never hardcode participant data, debug data or sample results inside `src/`. Test data
   lives only in `packages/engine/test/`. Real-looking names are never used; use
   identifiers like `P-TEST-01`.
4. Never recalculate and overwrite an imported Fusion authorization. Values the engine
   computes are always tagged `source: "derived"` with a `method` string.
5. Never mark something compliant when its rule status is OPEN or PARTIAL: emit severity
   `REVIEW`, not silence.
6. Use exact integer minute arithmetic. Only apply rounding where the spec names the
   rounding function (`ceil`, `trunc(x + 0.99)`, `floor`).
7. TypeScript `strict: true`. No `any`. No `// @ts-ignore`. No default exports.
8. Complete every function you start. No `TODO`, no stubs, no placeholder returns.
9. Before finishing any task run, in `packages/engine`:
   `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx vitest run`. Both must pass. Paste the summary lines of both
   into your final message.
10. Commit on the branch the prompt names, with the commit message the prompt gives. Never
    commit to `main` directly and never push with `--force`.

## Pinned versions (do not upgrade)
- Node 22 LTS
- typescript 5.9.3
- vitest 3.2.4
- luxon 3.5.0 and @types/luxon 3.4.2
- Package manager: npm (workspaces). No pnpm, no yarn.

## Style
- One concept per file, files under 300 lines.
- Pure functions; no module-level mutable state; no I/O in `src/`.
- Dates: ISO strings `YYYY-MM-DD`; months `YYYY-MM`; times are local
  `America/Chicago` and converted with luxon only inside `src/calendar/time.ts`.
